From dad20f81b2f386af7ae158df4b48e30e0f808a54 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qzshch <qzshch@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 17:30:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 04/14] feat(models): host-side block retrieval index and
 selector

First retrieval-tiering module (pure host logic, no GPU state):
- RetrievalIndex tracks dense 128-token blocks over one sequence, stores
  per-(layer, kv_head) content-domain mean-K for full blocks, rewinds with
  truncate_to, and scores a GQA-summed query mean against each block by
  head-averaged, layer-averaged cosine.
- select_blocks turns per-block scores into the device working-set block
  list: mandatory blocks first (query-span overlap), then sink prefix and
  recent suffix, then descending top-k, all charged against one budget.

The selection feeds KVAddressSpaceStore::apply_device_placement; block ->
page-set translation and the query accumulator (engine-side capture) come
with the integration step.

